  "body": "## Problem and behavior\n\nChat cached thread lists, messages, read markers and selected-thread preferences without account scope. Failed refetches could leave previously fetched previews and messages visible. Scope related query keys and browser preferences by account, remount drafts on account switch, hide stale content/composer on errors, and withdraw a denied conversation from the shared unread badge cache. Mutation completion uses the submitted thread ID.\n\n**Depends on #390**, then #386/#382 and the documented social stack. Draft; leave unmerged and undeployed.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **28 focused tests passed** in the child worktree: real QueryClient denial/account-switch journeys, read-marker isolation and existing selector/read-state regressions.\n- Focused ESLint and unchanged catalog audit passed on identical source files.\n- Repository application typecheck passed, exit 0. An extra test-inclusive TypeScript invocation failed in unchanged test files; its log is retained and is not described as a passing check or an executed baseline.\n- The initial hosted model job failed during fixture startup; #390 repairs TCP readiness without weakening assertions. The child branch includes that repair. [Social CI](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/actions/runs/35052928324) and [full UI CI](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/actions/runs/35052928363) passed at `8b7daf9c81da8e2c1d1fe8f785371fb33d174078`; backend/mobile jobs were scoped out and are not counted as passes.\n- CI now includes these component tests and tracks the changed chat files.\n\nDetails, actual commands, hashes and limitations: `docs/social/chat-client-isolation.md` and `docs/social/evidence/chat-client-isolation/`.\n\n## Compatibility, flags and rollback\n\nNo API/schema changes. This existing-chat security repair does not enable the social preview; production social flags remain off. Legacy unscoped read markers remain stored but are not assigned to an unproven account owner, so some chats initially appear unread. Scoped data is additive and survives UI pause. Retain the safe backend reader and write guard when rolling back; restoring shared cache keys would restore the demonstrated defect.\n\nExisting active polling (threads 10s/messages 3s) governs when a client learns of remote revocation; browser scheduling/connectivity can delay it. No promise to retract delivered content. New-chat selection still follows the existing mutual-friend flow; canonical selector integration, message idempotency, pagination, native/full-app journeys and the wider social cutover remain incomplete. No product-conversion claim, deployment or flag activation.\n",
